# EnvPilot run preferences

## While a run is in progress

- Change nothing. Propose the change, then wait for my approval.
- Never adjust timeouts, waits, or config without asking first.

## Watchers

- Tie the watcher to the app so it stops when EnvPilot closes or is force-closed.
- Track `python.exe` whose command line contains `EnvPilot_github\EnvPi`. The
  `powershell.exe` host launched by `EnvPilot.bat` exits early, so watching that PID
  stops the watcher while the deploy is still running.
- Cap the watcher at 5 minutes unless I say otherwise, and print why it stopped.
- Filter out `tokens:` lines and `msedgedriver!` / `GetHandleVerifier` stack frames.

## Reading logs

- `Action failed: No active KIAS DEV & TEST DESKTOP session found` immediately after Deploy
  is the normal `focus_desktop` probe before CASE C, not a failure. Do not report it as one.
- A watcher started mid-run replays earlier lines. Check timestamps before treating a
  match as new.

## Before blaming the code

Runs on identical code both succeed and fail depending on Citrix state — on 25 Aug, four of
ten runs passed with no code change between them. Confirm with `git status` and
`git diff HEAD` that code actually changed before attributing a failure to it.

## Reporting a failure

State the failing log line verbatim, the session ID, whether the start was warm or cold, and
whether a build was submitted.
